# Scanner

`scripts/scan-t2-host.sh` is read-only. Keep it that way.

- No sudo, no network, no package installs, no writes under `/etc` or `/sys`.
- Never read or print `product_serial`, `product_uuid`, `board_serial`, Wi-Fi connection profiles, or `nmcli` secrets.
- Print device ids, driver names, service state, and firmware version strings. Redact MAC addresses, UUIDs, and IPv6 link-local addresses.
- Exit 0 when the report was printed, including when an optional tool is missing.
- New checks belong in a `[flags]` line of the form `flag name=yes|no`.
- SPDX header stays `Apache-2.0`.
